Step 1 - Maven Clean
Step 2 - Maven Package

Step 3 - Create the input directory if it doesn't already exist:
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force "jpackage-build\input" | Out-Null

Remove files left over from previous builds:
Remove-Item "jpackage-build\input\*" -Recurse -Force

Copy the application JAR
Copy-Item "target\hardware-monitor-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar" "jpackage-build\input\"

Copy the runtime dependencies
Copy-Item "target\dependency\*.jar" "jpackage-build\input\"

Remove the previous debug application image
Remove-Item "jpackage-build\output\EcoScan-debug\EcoScan" -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

Generate EcoScan.exe

jpackage `
    --type app-image `
    --name EcoScan `
    --input "jpackage-build\input" `
    --dest "jpackage-build\output\EcoScan-debug" `
    --main-jar "hardware-monitor-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar" `
    --main-class "com.example.monitortest.Main" `
    --win-console


explorer "jpackage-build\output\EcoScan-debug\EcoScan"

Create a release build without the debugging console
jpackage `
    --type app-image `
    --name EcoScan `
    --input "jpackage-build\input" `
    --dest "jpackage-build\output\EcoScan-release" `
    --main-jar "hardware-monitor-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar" `
    --main-class "com.example.monitortest.Main"

The resulting executable will be located at:
jpackage-build\output\EcoScan-release\EcoScan\EcoScan.exe

If that output folder already contains an EcoScan application image, remove or rename the old image first

Create a portable ZIP (optional)
Compress-Archive `
    -Path "jpackage-build\output\EcoScan-release\EcoScan" `
    -DestinationPath "jpackage-build\output\EcoScan-portable.zip" `
    -Force